+---
+id: dl-002-availability-query-semantics
+type: decision-log
+title: "Availability query semantics"
+status: pending
+---
+
+# Availability query semantics
+
+## Context
+The desk needs to see what can still be rented over a period, optionally for one kind of equipment.
+
+## Decision
+- `availability({ start, end, kind? })` returns the ids of the items free for the whole period, sorted
+  with the default string order (deterministic).
+- The period follows dl-001: half-open `[start, end)`, UTC midnight ISO strings, `end` after `start`;
+  an invalid period throws, as in `quote`. An item booked on the day the period ends, or ending on the
+  day it starts, is still free.
+- An omitted `kind` means every kind; a `kind` that is neither `board` nor `sail` throws rather than
+  silently returning an empty list.
+- No match returns an empty array.
+
+## Consequences
+Availability and `book` share the same overlap rule, so an id listed can be booked for that period.
